/* The full-system reason the slow eigenvalue stays at -b: the O(1) Schur correction
 * rho^T A^{-1} c = 0.  The sympy proof (verify_freq_mode.py) does it WITHOUT inverting
 * A, using two structural facts:
 *   (i)  row 7 of A is  e6^T A = -1.5*Vg * e1^T   (from F7 = Pref - 1.5 Vg id),
 *   (ii) c[6] = 0                                  (dF7/d(dw) = 0, Power Lock),
 *   (iii) rho^T = -1.5*kappa*Vg * e1^T             (Variant-S row, = kappa * (-dPmeas/dz)).
 * Let u = A^{-1} c, i.e. A u = c.  Reading off component 7 (index 6) of A u = c:
 *   (e6^T A) u = c[6]   =>   (-1.5 Vg) * (e1^T u) = c[6] = 0   =>   e1^T u = 0  (Vg>0).
 * Then rho^T u = (-1.5 kappa Vg) * (e1^T u) = 0.
 *
 * We encode it division-free: let U1 := e1^T u = u[1] (first component of A^{-1}c).
 * Hypotheses: the row-7 reading  (-3/2*Vg)*U1 = c6,  the Power Lock  c6 = 0,  Vg>0,
 * and rho^T u = (-3/2*kappa*Vg)*U1.  Conclude rho^T u = 0  (= kappa * K). */
Problem
  \forall Vg \forall kappa \forall U1 \forall c6 \forall rhoTu
  ( Vg > 0
    & (-3/2*Vg)*U1 = c6        /* component-7 of A u = c, using e6^T A = -1.5 Vg e1^T */
    & c6 = 0                   /* c[6] = dF7/d(dw) = 0  (Power Lock)                  */
    & rhoTu = (-3/2*kappa*Vg)*U1   /* rho^T u, using rho^T = -1.5 kappa Vg e1^T       */
    -> rhoTu = 0 )
End.
